ock Elements (Group 15, 16, 17 & 18)","exam":"Engineering","examName":"KVPY","q":"When chlorine gas is passed through an aqueous solution of $\\mathrm{KBr}$, the solution turns orange brown due to the formation of","options":["$\\mathrm{KCl}$","$\\mathrm{HCl}$","$\\mathrm{HBr}$","$\\mathrm{Br}_{2}$"],"answer":3,"solution":"$2 \\mathrm{KBr}+\\mathrm{Cl}_{2} \\longrightarrow 2 \\mathrm{KCl}+\\mathrm{Br}_{2}$ (brown)","difficulty":"Medium","source":"KVPY 2011 (SA)","_marksId":"6174d21320ef0a8635939c36"},{"id":51296,"subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"p Block Elements (Group 15, 16, 17 & 18)","exam":"Engineering","examName":"KVPY","q":"The numbers of lone pair(s) on $\\mathrm{Xe}$ in $\\mathrm{XeF}_{2}$ and $\\mathrm{XeF}_{4}$ are, respectively,","options":["2 and 3","4 and 1","3 and 2","4 and 2"],"answer":2,"solution":"$\\mathrm{XeF}_{2} ;$ no. of $\\mathrm{lp}$ on $\\mathrm{Xe}=3\\operatorname{XeF}_{4}^{2} ;$ no. of $\\mathrm{lp}$ on $\\mathrm{Xe}=2$","difficulty":"Medium","source":"KVPY 2013 (SB/SX)","_marksId":"6174d2131c17803e6440e973"},{"id":51297,"subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"p Block Elements (Group 15, 16, 17 & 18)","exam":"Engineering","examName":"KVPY","q":"Ammonia is NOT produced in the reaction of","options":["$\\mathrm{NH}_{4} \\mathrm{Cl}$ with $\\mathrm{KOH}$","AIN with water","$\\mathrm{NH}_{4} \\mathrm{Cl}$ with $\\mathrm{NaNO}_{2}$","$\\mathrm{NH}_{4} \\mathrm{Cl}$ with $\\mathrm{Ca}(\\mathrm{OH})_{2}$"],"answer":2,"solution":"$\\quad \\mathrm{NH}_{4} \\mathrm{Cl}+\\mathrm{NaNO}_{2} \\longrightarrow \\mathrm{NaCl}+\\mathrm{N}_{2}+2 \\mathrm{H}_{2} \\mathrm{O}$","difficulty":"Medium","source":"KVPY 2014 (SA)","_marksId":"6174d213754184477f71755c"},{"id":51298,"subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"p Block Elements (Group 15, 16, 17 & 18)","exam":"Engineering","examName":"KVPY","q":"The correct structure of $\\mathrm{PCl}_{3} \\mathrm{~F}_{2}$ is-","options":["<img src=\"/api/proxy-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Ffirebasestorage.googleapis.com%2Fv0%2Fb%2Fquantrexacade